e,v=ev(38,'1–13','Vyāsa asks Gṛtsamada’s later conduct. Sages now honour/select him for sacrifices and remember him at Gaṇeśa worship, fulfilling recognition. Still devoted, he sneezes mightily and sees a radiant red fearsome child. Initially fearful he questions origin and parents. Child says he arose from Gṛtsamada’s sneeze, calls him both father and mother, and asks a few days’ care.',[('Vyāsa',S),('Brahmā',D),('Gṛtsamada',S),('Future Gṛtsamada son',A),('Honouring sages','FAMILY')],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Divine son promise follows Gṛtsamada recognition.',outcome='Actual sneeze-born child confirms origin; no biological human mother assigned.')
tripura=names['Future Gṛtsamada son'];names['Tripura']=tripura
entityrows[tripura]['name']='Tripura';entityrows[tripura]['aliases']=[{'name':'Future Gṛtsamada son','evidence_ids':[e]}]
rel('Tripura','child_of','Gṛtsamada',e,'SNEEZE_EMANATION');val('Tripura','origin','Arises from Gṛtsamada’s sneeze; child calls sage both father and mother38.12–13.',e)
e,v=ev(38,'14–22','Newborn promises to conquer three worlds and subdue Indra. Gṛtsamada, fearful and joyful, decides his own Gaṇānāṃ tvā mantra will bring desired boon and his own fame. He initiates child with steady Gaṇeśa-focused practice. Child goes to forest, stands on one toe without food and with controlled senses. After15,000 years (sārdhāyuta), fire from his mouth terrifies gods and lower-world daityas.',[('Gṛtsamada',S),('Tripura',A),('Indra',D),('Gaṇānāṃ tvā Vedic mantra',T),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Tripura austerity-fire',W)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Newborn ambition motivates initiation and ascetic practice.',outcome='Long mantra practice produces terrifying fire and divine response.')
rel('Gṛtsamada','initiates','Tripura',e);rel('Gṛtsamada','teaches_mantra','Gaṇānāṃ tvā Vedic mantra',e);rel('Tripura','worships','Gaṇeśa',e)
power('Tripura',e,v,mechanism='Mouth fire afflicts directions and terrifies gods/daityas after15,000 years practice.',trigger='Ascetic mantra practice.')
e_aust=e
e,v=ev(38,'23–36','Gaṇeśa appears radiant with four arms, axe, lotus, mālā and modakas. Trunk roar/radiance disturb child, who bows and asks a gentler form. Deity draws in brilliance, identifies himself as object of meditation and offers boons, declaring cosmic transcendence. Child thanks him, calls father blessed, says infancy limits praise and asks grant.',[('Tripura',A),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Gṛtsamada',S),('Gaṇeśa axe',W),('Gaṇeśa lotus',C),('Gaṇeśa mālā',C),('Modakas',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Successful austerity attracts personal divine appearance.',outcome='Gentler form makes desired-boon dialogue possible.')
for a in ['Gaṇeśa axe','Gaṇeśa lotus','Gaṇeśa mālā','Modakas']:rel('Gaṇeśa','bears',a,e)
e,v=ev(38,'37–40','Child requests power to draw/conquer three worlds; perpetual subjection of gods, dānavas, gandharvas, humans, serpents, rākṣasas, sages, kinnaras and cāraṇas; every mental desire fulfilled; Indra and guardians serving him; earthly enjoyment and final liberation; fame of penance-city as wish-giving Gaṇeśapura.',[('Tripura',A),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Indra',D),('Tripura Gaṇeśapura',L),('Gods',C),('Gandharvas',C),('Nāgas',C),('Kinnaras',C),('Cāraṇas',C),('Dānavas',C),('Rākṣasas',C),('Humans',C),('Sages',C),('World guardians',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Deity offers grant.',outcome='Universal domination, desire fulfilment, enjoyment/liberation and site request stated.')
e_req=e
e,v=ev(38,'41–46','Gaṇeśa promises three-world conquest, no fear and all subjects, grants iron/gold/silver three cities, freely moving and unbreakable by gods except Śaṅkara. He names child Tripura. When Śiva breaks his city complex with one arrow, he gains liberation then; all other desires fulfilled by grace. Gaṇeśa vanishes; Tripura grieves separation, rejoices at boons and begins conquest.',[('Tripura',A),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Śiva',D),('Tripura iron city',C),('Tripura gold city',C),('Tripura silver city',C),('Tripura three-city complex',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Domination request receives detailed grant and exception.',outcome='Mobile city boon and one-arrow liberation condition drive forthcoming war.')
p=power('Tripura',e,v,typ='BOON',grant='Gaṇeśa',requested='Three-world conquest/subjection of all listed beings, Indra/guardians as servants, all mental desires, enjoyment, final liberation and Gaṇeśapura fame.',granted='Conquest/subjection/no fear; freely moving iron/gold/silver cities invulnerable to gods except Śaṅkara; Tripura name; other desires affirmed.',restrictions='Śaṅkara explicitly excepted from city invulnerability.',trigger='Śiva breaking the city complex with a single arrow brings liberation at that time.',austerity_or_circumstances='Gaṇānāṃ tvā practice, toe-stance, fasting/sense restraint15,000 years.',notes='Not the standard recalled Brahmā Tripura boon: this witness’s actual Gaṇeśa request/grant/exception retained.')
