e_aust_gods=e
e,v=ev(40,'42–57','Gods’ hymn praises supreme causality, cosmic creation/preservation/dissolution, all boons, obstruction removal, knowledge and contrasting devotee/nondevotee outcomes. Deity pleased by hymn+austerity offers boon. They request killing Tripura who seized all offices, citing his own divine protection and taking refuge. He promises removal of all fear; names hymn Saṅkaṭanāśana, granting all wishes to readers/hearers and no distress to three-sandhyā reciters, then vanishes.',[('Gods',C),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Tripura',A),('Saṅkaṭanāśana hymn',T),('Saṅkaṭanāśana practitioners',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Collective dispossession is taken to boon-giver.',outcome='Fear-removal promise and conditional hymn efficacy granted; kill request not yet enacted.')
p=power('Gods',e,v,typ='BOON',grant='Gaṇeśa',requested='Kill Tripura and free gods from distress/seized offices.',granted='Remove all fear from the terrifying enemy.',austerity_or_circumstances='Long unspecified fast/breath restraint, varied postures, one-syllable practice and collective hymn.',notes='Requested killing vs granted fear removal kept distinct; actual counterstrategy follows41.')
