e,v=ev(41,'1–10','To Vyāsa’s inquiry Brahmā says Gaṇeśa visits Tripura in Brahmin form. Honoured with throne/worship, he identifies himself as Kalādhara, freely wandering all-knowing benefactor, and praises Tripura’s riches beyond divine worlds. Tripura challenges him to demonstrate an extraordinary art, promising desired gift even life and claiming never to speak falsely.',[('Vyāsa',S),('Brahmā',D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Kalādhara (Gaṇeśa disguise)',S),('Tripura',A),('Kailāsa',L),('Vaikuṇṭha',L),('Brahmaloka',L)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Gaṇeśa’s fear-removal promise prompts disguise strategy.',outcome='Demonstration-for-gift bargain accepted.')
