power('Gaṇeśa',e,v,mechanism='Appears as Brahmin Kalādhara to Tripura.',notes='Narrated deliberate disguise; not a separate biological sage identity.')
e,v=ev(41,'11–18','Kalādhara offers gold/silver/iron three-city complex, wish-giving, freely moving and unbreakable by gods/Gandharvas/humans/serpents, but eventual Śiva single-arrow breach destroys Tripura. Taking bow and fixing arrow, he creates airy cities with buildings/lakes/groves/birds. Māyā deludes Tripura who enters, roars and prides himself unsurpassed.',[('Kalādhara (Gaṇeśa disguise)',S),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Tripura',A),('Śiva',D),('Tripura three-city complex',C),('Tripura gold city',C),('Tripura silver city',C),('Tripura iron city',C),('Kalādhara bow',W),('Kalādhara arrow',W)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Art challenge creates occasion for renewed conditional city grant.',outcome='Cities actually constructed; recipient deluded into pride.')
power('Tripura',e,v,typ='BOON',grant='Gaṇeśa',granted='Gold/silver/iron mobile wish-giving cities, constructed by Kalādhara.',restrictions='Eventually Śiva’s single-arrow breach destroys Tripura; unbreakability against listed other beings.',mechanism='Kalādhara uses bow/arrow to construct cities and māyā deludes recipient.',notes='Repeated city-grant scene after38; not silently collapsed into a single scene.')
e,v=ev(41,'19–29','Tripura offers rare gift. Kalādhara requests the extraordinary wish-giving Gaṇeśa image he saw worshipped by Śiva at Kailāsa, promising to spread donor fame. Tripura dismisses Śiva as servant and promises retrieval. He gives ten villages, cattle, clothes/ornaments, pearls/gems/coral, blankets,100 male/female servants, fine horses and silver chariots with gold axles. Kalādhara accepts forced gifts and returns to āśrama, delighting wife/residents as this narrator’s formulation. Nārada reports all events to gods who wait.',[('Tripura',A),('Kalādhara (Gaṇeśa disguise)',S),('Śiva',D),('Cintāmaṇi image in Tripura war',D),('Kailāsa',L),('Nārada',S),('Gods',C),('Kalādhara’s reported wife/residents','FAMILY')],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Demonstrated art activates promised reward.',outcome='Image retrieval promise brings approaching conflict; gods await strategy.')
val('Kalādhara (Gaṇeśa disguise)','narrator_return_formulation','41.28 says returns to āśrama delighting wife/residents despite41.2 identification as disguised Gaṇeśa; no spouse identity supplied.',e)
e,v=ev(42,'1–14','Vyāsa asks about promised image. Tripura sends two messengers to Śiva at Mandāra demanding peaceful delivery of wish-giving Cintāmaṇi image or forced seizure, boasting all rare objects collected. Furious Śiva spares them because they are envoys, saying otherwise they would burn like Kāma; challenges Tripura to battle and says image cannot be won even after100 births. Envoys report refusal.',[('Vyāsa',S),('Brahmā',D),('Tripura',A),('Tripura’s two Śiva envoys','FAMILY'),('Śiva',D),('Mandāra',L),('Cintāmaṇi image in Tripura war',D),('Manobhava',D)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Image bargain prompts ultimatum.',outcome='Envoy immunity preserves messengers; refusal makes war inevitable.')
e,v=ev(42,'15–25','Enraged Tripura sends vast fourfold army to Mandāra and follows mounted on mind-speed aerial city complex, adorned in jewel-armour, earrings/crown/ornaments, with powerful bow, quiver, tortoise-type shield, sword and divine śakti. Gandharvas/Apsarases, bards and Cāraṇas precede him. Śiva hears approach, explicitly worships, bows and circumambulates Gaṇeśa in this passage, then marches with troops and trident.',[('Tripura',A),('Tripura army','ARMY'),('Śiva',D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Mandāra',L),('Tripura three-city complex',C),('Tripura jewel-armour',C),('Tripura bow',W),('Tripura quiver',W),('Tripura tortoise shield',W),('Tripura sword',W),('Tripura divine śakti',W),('Trident',W),('Gandharvas',C),('Apsarases',C),('Cāraṇas',C),('Bards','FAMILY')],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Śiva rejects image seizure.',outcome='Two armies deploy;42 worship statement retained despite later contrary explanation.')
