e,v=ev(42,'26–35','Noisy armies clash in dust and lose friend/enemy distinction. When dust settles, individual duels use prāsa, swords, sharpened arrows, ṛṣṭi, fists, axes, tomara and trees. Slaughter of foot/horse/chariot/elephant troops makes a river of blood. Śiva and city-mounted Tripura draw near while gods/daityas arrange individual duels whose names Brahmā promises next.',[('Śiva',D),('Tripura',A),('Tripura army','ARMY'),('Śiva attendants','ARMY'),('Prāsa spears',W),('Swords',W),('Arrows',W),('Ṛṣṭi spears',W),('Battle axes',W),('Tomara',W),('Battle trees',W),('Tripura three-city complex',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Deployments meet in general combat.',outcome='Mass battle becomes distinct named duels.')
