e,v=ev(43,'9–14','Pracaṇḍa fires nine arrows; Kārttikeya cuts them before arrival and strikes with five, making Pracaṇḍa faint/fall. Nandin’s five sharpened arrows similarly drop Caṇḍa. Bhīmakāya shoots ten at Puṣpadanta who cuts all, hits with three and drops him. Bhṛśuṇḍī drops Kālakūṭa with five arrows.',[('Pracaṇḍa',A),('Ṣaṇmukha/Kārttikeya',D),('Nandin',F),('Caṇḍa',A),('Bhīmakāya',A),('Puṣpadanta',F),('Bhṛśuṇḍī',S),('Kālakūṭa',A),('Arrows',W)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Named duels proceed through arrow-counterarrow exchanges.',outcome='Four daitya opponents incapacitated; deaths not asserted when fall/faint is stated.')
e,v=ev(43,'15–21','Vīrabhadra fires four at Vajradaṃṣṭra, who blocks and replies with three. Vīrabhadra cuts those with three then drops opponent with three. Indra drops daitya minister with vajra. Unnamed son advances with sword on Jayanta; Jayanta cuts sword with arrow and hits with three, causing blood-vomit and unconscious fall. Daityas flee and victorious Pramathas pursue.',[('Vīrabhadra',F),('Vajradaṃṣṭra',A),('Indra',D),('Indra vajra',W),('Tripura’s unnamed minister',A),('Tripura’s unnamed fighting son',A),('Jayanta',F),('Arrows',W),('Swords',W),('Pramathas','ARMY')],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Individual counterattacks defeat daitya champions.',outcome='Initial divine victory breaks enemy troops.')
e,v=ev(43,'22–29','Tripura personally approaches Śiva in his cities, moves from physical weapons to astras, and releases Vāruṇa weapon: torrential rain/mist and lightning obscure battlefield and stonefall/wind rout Śiva’s army. Śiva releases Vāyavya, breaking clouds, whirling daitya troops, stripping hats/feathers, crushing vehicles and uprooting vegetation. Tripura counters wind with Pannaga weapon.',[('Tripura',A),('Śiva',D),('Tripura three-city complex',C),('Vāruṇa astra',W),('Vāyavya astra',W),('Pannaga astra',W),('Śiva attendants','ARMY'),('Tripura army','ARMY')],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Tripura intervenes after retinue defeats.',outcome='Rain→wind→serpent sequence changes battlefield advantage.')
power('Tripura',e,v,mechanism='Vāruṇa rain/mist/stonefall disrupts Śiva army.',counter='Śiva’s Vāyavya breaks clouds and attacks enemy ranks.')
power('Śiva',e,v,mechanism='Vāyavya wind breaks clouds, whirls/crushes enemy troops and uproots trees.',counter='Tripura counters with Pannaga astra.')
e,v=ev(43,'30–38','Tripura shoots Anala-enchanted arrow causing coal-rain and flames. From flames arises huge hunger-driven fanged roaring man, tongue100yojanas, nose-wind hurling elephants, who devours Śiva’s troops. They beg Śiva’s protection. He reassures, suppresses fire with Parjanya astra and drops man with one arrow, but man rises and resumes eating. Pramathas flee stumbling/shaking; unsupported Śiva retreats into cave.',[('Tripura',A),('Śiva',D),('Anala astra',W),('Parjanya astra',W),('Śiva single arrow (fire-man)',W),('Fire-born devouring man',A),('Pramathas','ARMY'),('Śiva retreat cave',L)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Countered wind is followed by fire weapon and persistent combatant.',outcome='Rain suppresses fire but arrow fails to stop revived man; Śiva retreats.')
power('Tripura',e,v,mechanism='Anala arrow brings coal-rain/fire and a devouring giant.',counter='Parjanya quenches fire; arrow drops giant temporarily but he rises and continues devouring.',notes='Weapon extinguishing and combatant revival are distinct outcomes.')
power('Fire-born devouring man',e,v,mechanism='Hundred-yojana tongue, elephant-hurling nose-wind, army-devouring hunger and recovery after arrow fall.',counter='Śiva’s arrow only temporarily drops him; resumed attack forces retreat.')
e,v=ev(43,'39–47','Ṣaḍānana and other heroes follow retreating Śiva. Tripura seeks to seize solitary Girijā at Kailāsa; she sees approach, goes to father and asks protection. Father hides her in inaccessible secret cave. Tripura comes to Himalayan mountain but cannot find her; sees Cintāmaṇi image, seizes it and returns victorious toward lower world. Image vanishes in his hand; he takes this as ominous, re-enters city distressed.',[('Ṣaṇmukha/Kārttikeya',D),('Śiva',D),('Tripura',A),('Girijā',D),('Girijā’s father in43',F),('Kailāsa',L),('Himalayan mountain',L),('Girijā hiding cave',L),('Cintāmaṇi image in Tripura war',D)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Divine retreat exposes Girijā to capture attempt.',outcome='Girijā protected; stolen image vanishes, denying promised transfer.')
rel('Girijā','child_of','Girijā’s father in43',e,'EXPLICIT_UNNAMED_FATHER');rel('Girijā’s father in43','protects','Girijā',e)
power('Cintāmaṇi image in Tripura war',e,v,mechanism='Vanishes from Tripura’s hand during departure.',notes='Actual disappearance; agency/motive not separately spoken in this verse.')
e,v=ev(44,'1–13','Vyāsa asks defeat remedy. Śiva worries about earth deprived of svāhā/svadhā and gods’ restoration, welcomes Nārada and reports routed gods in unknown locations and thousands of countered astras. Nārada reverently acknowledges all-knowledge/power, reflects and offers requested advice.',[('Vyāsa',S),('Brahmā',D),('Śiva',D),('Nārada',S),('Gods',C),('Tripura',A)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Retreat prompts reflection and adviser arrival.',outcome='Śiva solicits a remedy, acknowledging battlefield failure.')
e,v=ev(44,'14–23','Nārada says Śiva failed to worship Gaṇeśa before battle and must now propitiate him, get boon and win. He recalls Tripura’s immunity except Maheśvara and prescribes one arrow to split three mobile cities. Śiva agrees and remembers earlier one-/six-syllable initiation, saying battle preoccupation caused no recitation/remembrance. Nārada again urges worship; Śiva leaves for austerity.',[('Śiva',D),('Nārada',S),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Tripura',A),('Single-syllable Gaṇeśa mantra',T),('Six-syllable Gaṇeśa mantra',T),('Tripura three-city complex',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Nārada gives omission-of-worship explanation and exact boon counter.',outcome='Śiva accepts remembrance/initiation remedy; source discrepancy retained.')
variant('siva-prebattle-worship','42.24–25 explicitly narrates Śiva worship/bow/circumambulation of Gaṇeśa before march;44.14/21–22 attributes defeat to omitted worship/recitation/remembrance.45.12–13 and46.2 repeat omission explanation. Source-local sequence conflict remains OPEN; no invented distinction between perfunctory/proper worship.',e)
d['variants_and_conflicts'][-1]['evidence_ids'].append(e_worship)
e,v=ev(44,'24–35','In Daṇḍakāraṇya Śiva sits lotus-postured with restrained senses and focused japa/meditation, practicing100years. A five-faced ten-armed figure with moon brow, skull garland, serpent adornments, crown/armlets and ten unspecified weapons emerges from his mouth, radiant beyond sun/fire/moon. Śiva wonders whether doubled himself, disguised Tripura, dream, or Gaṇeśa. Figure identifies as inwardly contemplated obstacle-remover, cosmic lord pleased with austerity and invites all desired boons.',[('Śiva',D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Five-faced Gaṇeśa before Śiva',D),('Daṇḍakāraṇya',L),('Tripura',A),('Ten unspecified Gaṇeśa weapons',W),('Gaṇeśa skull garland',C),('Gaṇeśa serpent ornaments',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Accepted advice leads to renewed ascetic japa.',outcome='Personal appearance and boon invitation after100years.')
rel('Five-faced Gaṇeśa before Śiva','appearance_of','Gaṇeśa',e);rel('Five-faced Gaṇeśa before Śiva','bears','Ten unspecified Gaṇeśa weapons',e)
e_siva_aust=e
e,v=ev(45,'1–8','Asked by a sage/Brahmā’s narrative framing what Śiva requested, Śiva praises his ten eyes/arms and five heads/faces as fulfilled by vision/worship, then Gaṇeśa as origin of elements/senses/gods/sages/ancestors/Viṣṇu-Brahmā-Śiva and cosmic functions. Brahmā’s first-person speech says he spoke at Śiva’s command, deriving Gaṇeśa name from lordship of gaṇas and Oṃ as primary letter-seed; deity assents.',[('Questioning sage in45',S),('Brahmā',D),('Śiva',D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Oṃ',T),('Vasus',C),('Sādhyas',C),('Ancestors',C),('Yakṣas',C),('Gandharvas',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Boon invitation prompts praise/name explanation.',outcome='Name derivation and assent precede grace request; first-person switch preserved.')
e,v=ev(45,'9–14','Śiva grants Gaṇeśa-related remembrance/worship efficacy: remembering at tasks gives obstacle-free completion; Gaṇeśa is to be worshipped first in Śaiva/Gāṇapatya/Vaiṣṇava/Śākta/Saura and Vedic/worldly auspicious/inauspicious activities.45.10 lacks secure negative in without-remembrance clause and is not emended. Śiva says neglected worship/bows/remembrance caused defeat and requests forgiveness and victory at battles. He expresses that nondevotees become dull/poor and devotees gain wish-granting success.',[('Śiva',D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Gaṇeśa remembrancers in45',C),('Śaiva ritual tradition','TRADITION'),('Gāṇapatya ritual tradition','TRADITION'),('Vaiṣṇava ritual tradition','TRADITION'),('Śākta ritual tradition','TRADITION'),('Saura ritual tradition','TRADITION')],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Śiva acknowledges omission and asks forgiveness/victory.',outcome='First-worship efficacy spoken; personal request stated with textual uncertainty.')
e_siva_req=e
power('Gaṇeśa remembrancers in45',e,v,typ='BOON',grant='Śiva',granted='Obstacle-free task completion on remembering Gaṇeśa; first worship across stated ritual traditions.',trigger='Task-start remembrance and first worship.',notes='Śiva is the grant-speaker45.9. Defective without-remembrance clause10 remains unresolved; no exclusive negative proposition asserted.')
variant('chapter45-without-remembrance','45.10 printed without-remembrance clause lacks secure negative; retain clear positive remembrance efficacy9 and mandatory first-worship11, no conjectural translation10.',e)
e,v=ev(45,'15–18','Gaṇeśa promises Śiva his arrival whenever remembered, and instructs enchanting one arrow with deity’s name-seed to bring down three cities by his radiance and reduce daitya to ash. He teaches thousand names granting victory/wishes; war-time recitation kills daityas swiftly, three-sandhyā recitation fulfils all desired wishes.',[('Gaṇeśa',D),('Śiva',D),('Tripura',A),('Tripura three-city complex',C),('Gaṇeśa name-seed arrow',W),('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma (Upāsanā46)',T),('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Forgiveness/victory request receives practical boon strategy.',outcome='Remembered appearance, seed-arrow and war hymn prescribed; actual destruction still future.')
rel('Gaṇeśa','teaches','Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma (Upāsanā46)',e);rel('Śiva','receives','Gaṇeśa name-seed arrow',e)
p=power('Śiva',e,v,typ='BOON',grant='Gaṇeśa',requested='Forgiveness for omitted worship/remembrance and victory in battles.',granted='Gaṇeśa arrives whenever remembered; single name-seed-enchanted arrow uses divine radiance to break cities/burn Tripura; thousand-name war-recitation guidance.',austerity_or_circumstances='100years lotus-seat japa in Daṇḍakāraṇya with restrained senses and focused meditation.',trigger='Remembrance for divine arrival; enchanting arrow with name-seed; thousand-name recitation in battle.',notes='Actual request/grant separated from destruction yet to occur.')
p['evidence_ids'] += [e_siva_req,e_siva_aust];p['field_evidence']['requested']=[e_siva_req];p['field_evidence']['austerity_or_circumstances']=[e_siva_aust]
power('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',e,v,typ='BOON',grant='Gaṇeśa',granted='Victory/swift daitya defeat when recited in war; all desired wishes on three-sandhyā recitation.',trigger='War recitation or three-sandhyā recitation, as respective outcomes.')
e,v=ev(45,'19–23','Śiva worships rejoicing, installs Mahāgaṇeśa and builds a high strong temple, satisfies gods/sages/Siddhas and gives Brahmin gifts, worships/bows again and proclaims city Maṇipūra. Gaṇeśa and assembled gods/sages vanish. Śiva returns with attendants, Gandharvas/Yakṣas/divine women and tells Girijā; gods/sages with spouses rejoice, treating Tripura as already dead and their offices regained in anticipation.',[('Śiva',D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Mahāgaṇeśa (Śiva installation)',D),('Maṇipūra (Śiva installation site)',L),('Gods',C),('Sages',C),('Siddhis',C),('Gandharvas',C),('Yakṣas',C),('Divine women','FAMILY'),('Girijā',D),('Tripura',A)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Personal grant prompts installation and hopeful report.',outcome='Actual temple established; enemy death/office restoration only anticipated at this point.')
rel('Śiva','installs','Mahāgaṇeśa (Śiva installation)',e);rel('Mahāgaṇeśa (Śiva installation)','installed_at','Maṇipūra (Śiva installation site)',e)
